NUM-50: apply a link API mass flux under STEADY routing as flux / flow

Under STEADY routing a conduit stores no pollutant: findSFLinkQual() gives it
the upstream node's concentration and the conduit passes on c * q per second.
The API mass-flux block used the dynamic-wave mixing formula instead,
dc = F * dt / (V + q * dt), and booked all of F as external inflow, so only
the fraction q * dt / (V + q * dt) of the booked mass ever left the conduit.
Change the concentration by F / q and book exactly what that carries; with no
flow through the conduit the flux is not applied (and not booked).

Requires: CRASH-12

Requires: NUM-01
Requires: NUM-45
Requires: NUM-48

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b,
after CRASH-12_swmm530.patch:
